# Ancient Mummy, the August head (ticket 45): a round head wrapped in dusty linen bandages that cross at all angles in light and old-brown
# bands, a dark slot left open across the eyes with two pale dead eyes and small pupils in it, a nose and a chin under the wrapping and loose
# ends of bandage hanging off the back, the side and the cheek.
# Frame (the soldier's head_top socket, ticket 43): the origin is the socket, 1.815 m over the soles; the head faces +Z, +Y is up. The
# size and the height come from the head part (content/parts/mummy_head.sdf): normalized to the common size, the chin 4 cm lower than
# phase 1's (at 1.525 m, over the neck's top at 1.569 whose stub is inside it). The head turns on the Head bone, 0.25 m under the origin.
# The eyes are part of the head (a pale sphere and a pupil each), no eye part.
format 1

# No collider (the hit shape of the head is a number in the registry), and never culled before 200 m: the head is what reads at range
collider none
cull 200

Detail detail=0.571
    Part part=mummy_head
